  "description": "Invented by a restaurant owner from Greece, Memphis dry ribs are bathed in vinegar while being grilled over smoky charcoal, then coated with an earthy, herbal rub once they're done cooking. Just don't let the name mislead you: There's nothing dry about these babies.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: baby back ribs → St. Louis-cut spare ribs\n\nNotes: These ribs are best cooked a few feet directly over charcoal. If that's not possible in your grill or smoker, then they can be cooked over indirect heat to keep the bottom of the ribs from burning.",
